            <ArticleTitle>Short interactive workshops reduce variability in contouring treatment volumes for spine stereotactic body radiation therapy: Experience with the ESTRO FALCON programme and EduCase™ training tool.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0167-8140(17)32692-0</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.radonc.2017.10.038</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the results of 4, 2-h contouring workshops on target volume definition for spinal stereotactic radiotherapy. They combined traditional teaching methods with a web-based contouring/contour-analysis platform and led to a significant reduction in delineation variability. Short, interactive workshops can reduce interobserver variability in spine SBRT target volume delineation.</AbstractText>
